Use shared response components in apps/api/docs/prototype/swagger.yaml

Generated on 2026-11-24. Apply AFTER swagger-recommended-changes.patch,
from the repository root:

  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/swagger-recommended-changes.patch
  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/swagger-shared-responses.patch

Replaces 32 inline response blocks with $ref links to 8 new
#/components/responses/ items, as in proposed-transfer-api.yaml:

- BadRequestChildDetails (400): GET /children, POST /children/search,
  POST /children/{ypid}/stages/
- BadRequestStageIdentifiers (400): GET, PATCH, PUT and DELETE on
  /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}
- BadRequestYpid (400): GET /children/{ypid}/, GET /children/{ypid}/stages/
- ChildIdentifierConflict (409): GET /children, POST /children,
  POST /children/search
- ChildNotFound (404): GET /children/{ypid}/, GET and POST
  /children/{ypid}/stages/
- ServerError (500): all 10 operations
- StageIdentifierConflict (409): GET, PATCH, PUT and DELETE on
  /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}
- StageNotEditable (403): PATCH, PUT and DELETE on
  /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}

Wording changes, agreed with the user on 2026-11-24:

- POST /children/search 409: "CYPID" corrected to "OYPID", matching
  the other two routes.
- BadRequestChildDetails no longer refers to "the request body", since
  GET /children has none.
- BadRequestStageIdentifiers adds GET's note that a mismatch between
  the child and the stageid gives 409 instead.
- StageNotEditable says "change" instead of naming PATCH, PUT or DELETE.

- POST /children: the ypid in the request body must be absent or null;
  any other value, including 0, gives 400. Previously the description
  said null or zero, with other values "disregarded", while the 400 said
  any non-null ypid was rejected.

Kept inline because each has its own meaning: POST /children 400 and
POST /children/{ypid}/stages/ 409.

